Root cause:
The bug was introduced due to a failure to correctly handle the Frame Error Concealment (FEC) mechanism in the decoder. Specifically, the previous implementation disabled FEC for most scenarios when it should have been active, particularly when packets were not concatenated. Additionally, the output buffer size calculation in the demo application was incorrect, which caused potential issues when decoding audio data, especially in the presence of lost packets. The patch rectifies these issues by ensuring FEC operations are enabled appropriately and adjusting the output buffer size calculation accordingly.
